WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.590
- [Narrator] In early May, gas prices,

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:03.970
which were already rising

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.050
due to lifted pandemic
restrictions shot up.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.210
And it had a lot to do with this.

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:12.000
- The biggest fuel pipeline
system in the United States.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.320
- Forced to shut down.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:14.650
- A suspected cyber attack.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.710
- A cyber extortion attempt.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:19.610
- [Narrator] On May 7th, the
nation's largest fuel pipeline,

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.780
Colonial, shut down for
six days in response

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.130
to a ransomware attack that
targeted the company's networks.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:29.170
- We have efforts underway
with the FBI and DOJ,

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:32.180
Department Of Justice, to disrupt them

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.970
and prosecute ransomware criminals.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.720
- [Narrator] The attack
drove panic consumers

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.330
to stockpile fuel, in
states heavily impacted

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.720
by the shutdown.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.640
Like North and South Carolina,
Georgia, and Virginia.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.370
This caused long lines and
shortages at gas stations.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.000
The colonial pipeline
cyber attack was the latest

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.370
high profile event to expose a threat

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.920
to aging vulnerable energy
infrastructure in the U.S.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:59.433
So just how vulnerable
are we to future attacks?

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:04.360
- Our energy infrastructure
is under attack

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:08.730
and has been under attack
for at least two decades now.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.600
So both from a physical
perspective, but also digital.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.020
- [Narrator] Theresa Payton
is a cybersecurity expert

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.800
and former White House
chief information officer

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.280
under the Bush administration.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.710
She says that the energy
infrastructure that fuels the U.S.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.700
is highly vulnerable to attacks like this.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:28.040
The country has around two
and a half million miles

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.450
of fuel pipelines.

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.290
And Colonial is a major
part of this network,

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.810
stretching from Texas to New Jersey.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:38.290
Each pipeline includes hundreds
of thousands of devices.

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:40.710
Sensors for readings,
valves that help control

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:43.750
flow and pressure, and
leak detection systems.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:47.200
Security experts say that
all are at risk in an attack.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.840
While most equipment isn't directly

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.680
connected to the internet,
the concern is that hackers

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.860
can penetrate digitized
tools or computer networks,

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:57.130
working their way into broader systems.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.640
Cyber criminals will
often infiltrate systems

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.130
through remote platform
hacking, email phishing schemes,

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.140
or through compromised
employee credentials.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.500
- Once they penetrate IT,
they study the traffic

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.110
of the accounts on the network,

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.740
and they learn how to hide in plain sight.

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:18.740
I liken it to somebody who
may be using rush hour traffic

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.070
to basically hide their car among hundreds

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.500
and thousands of vehicles in rush hour.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.090
It's hard to pick out the bad actor

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:29.350
when they're just kind of going

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.120
with the flow of the traffic.

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.840
- [Narrator] Once hackers are inside,

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:35.900
they can use malicious
code to lock up systems,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.560
or steal sensitive information
to extort their victims.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:41.260
And these type of cyber attacks

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.250
can have far reaching effects.

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.240
- You have seen after
hurricanes, where that has taken

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.920
part of our energy infrastructure offline

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.100
and sort of what the
downstream impacts are

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.570
for weeks and months afterwards.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:00.580
And so a cyber incident can have the same

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:05.580
or even more devastating
effects on our energy ecosystem.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.380
- [Narrator] So why are the nation's

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.450
most critical energy systems
so exposed to cyber crime?

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.150
Payton says that as older systems
are updated and digitized,

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:16.810
they've become more complex,

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.030
which hackers have taken advantage of.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:24.030
- We're integrating 5G
technology, smart grid technology.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.610
Sort of alternative and renewable

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.780
sustainable energy sources.

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:33.230
And each time you layer
on these new technologies,

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:36.080
these new technologies are unproven,

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:40.140
as far as how they will
stand up to a cyber attack.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.410
- [Narrator] In the U.S.,
there's also high demand

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.020
for energy to always be on and working.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.330
Which makes it difficult
for systems to be updated.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.070
Replacing outdated
systems is also expensive

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.810
and time consuming.

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.950
But it's not just aging infrastructure

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.400
and a lack of resources that expose

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.430
energy systems to cyber attacks.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:04.210
Experts say that hackers are
becoming increasingly organized

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:06.080
within the ransomware industry.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.550
- They'll use a combination
of burner phones,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.850
dark web forums, using handles in Reddit,

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:15.660
using code words when they're
trying to recruit people.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:19.800
And with more and more
Silicon Valley companies

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.980
rolling out encryption built in

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.490
as part of messaging platforms,
it makes it simpler for them

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:29.420
to just use commercially available tools.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.250
- [Narrator] After a successful
attack, cyber criminals

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.660
can demand payment in cryptocurrency,

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:37.880
which limits the ability of
law enforcement to track them.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.250
There's also been a growth
in insurance policies

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.290
that cover ransomware payments,

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:45.250
which could help boost
the illegal industry.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.450
Experts say attacks like the
one on the Colonial pipeline

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.840
are becoming more frequent.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.560
In 2020 energy companies
suffered the third largest number

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.070
of cyber attacks of any industry,

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:59.520
up from ninth place the previous year.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.440
But there's only a patchwork
of cybersecurity regulations

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.030
for energy companies.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:08.010
And the pipeline sector
is largely unregulated.

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:11.080
On May 10th, President Biden
said that his administration

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:14.540
was pursuing a global effort
to protect American companies

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:16.930
in infrastructure from ransomware attacks.

00:05:16.930 --> 00:05:19.470
- It begins with a hundred day sprint

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:23.520
to improve cyber security
in the electric sector.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.660
And we'll follow that
with similar initiatives

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.980
in natural gas pipelines,
water, and other sectors.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:33.080
In addition to companies
stepping up, we need to invest

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.810
to safeguard our critical infrastructure.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.290
- [Narrator] The colonial pipeline started

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.580
to resume operations on May 12th.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.130
but experts say the cyber
attack should still serve

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.367
as a wake-up call for the energy industry.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:47.367
(suspenseful music)

